/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The system provides features for creating new versions, viewing available versions, and maintaining the stored file history. Users can select a particular version and view its details, making it easier to keep track of changes made to a file over time. The system can also support comparison between different versions, allowing users to identify the changes made between them. These features are implemented through a simple and easy-to-use interface.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Another important part of the project is the recovery mechanism, which allows users to restore an earlier version of a file when required. If a user makes unwanted changes, replaces a file, or accidentally deletes it, an available previous version can be selected and restored. The project therefore combines version tracking and file recovery into a single system. It focuses on concepts such as file handling, data storage, version management, file comparison, and recovery mechanisms. Overall, the project provides a practical implementation of version control concepts in a general file management environment and demonstrates how files and their different versions can be stored, accessed, managed, and restored.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
